refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
mixedsnmp3_get stringhostname stringsecurity_name stringsecurity_level stringauth_protocol stringauth_passphrase stringprivacy_protocol stringprivacy_passphrase arraystringobject_id inttimeout-1 intretries-1
The snmp3_get function is used to read the value of an SNMP object specified by the object_id.

&reftitle.parameters;
hostname
The hostname of the SNMP agent (server). The hostname may be followed by a port, as in host:port; an IPv6 address must be enclosed in square brackets when used with a port ([::1]:161). Transport prefixes such as udp: or tcp: are not supported.
security_name
&snmp.parameter.security-name;
security_level
&snmp.parameter.security-level;
auth_protocol
&snmp.parameter.auth-protocol;
auth_passphrase
&snmp.parameter.auth-passphrase;
privacy_protocol
&snmp.parameter.privacy-protocol;
privacy_passphrase
&snmp.parameter.privacy-passphrase;
object_id
The SNMP object id.
timeout
The number of microseconds to wait for a response on each attempt, without backoff. A call can therefore last up to timeout multiplied by (retries + 1). The default, -1, uses the library default of 1 second.
retries
The number of times to retry if timeouts occur. The default, -1, uses the library default of 5 retries.

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;



   &snmp.changelog.privacy-protocol-aes;


    8.5.0

     Now throws a ValueError when the hostname
     contains null bytes or its length is equal to or greater than 128 bytes,
     when the port is negative or greater than 65535, when the security name is
     empty or contains null bytes, or when the timeout or retries values
     are lower than -1 or too large.


   &snmp.changelog.auth-protocol-sha2;
